CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
As `store_through_pointer_framing`, inside an atomic section: `*d = 8`,
with `d` pointing to `dA` or `dB`, frames the target it does not write back
over itself, and the old value is renamed with events off. Inside an atomic
section l2_thread_read_encoding ignored that and recorded the read anyway,
so with `d == &dB` main was seen reading `dA`, paired with the thread's
write of `dA` (made only when `d == &dB`): a race no execution has.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after.

See `atomic_section_store_through_pointer_race`: the thread writes `dA`
whatever `d` is, which must stay FAILED.
